=Watching Heart Signal with You=

7
00:00:25,380 --> 00:00:26,860
=Watching Heart Signal with You=

8
00:00:28,360 --> 00:00:29,480
(Heart's Answer)
We're back.

9
00:00:33,960 --> 00:00:36,280
Hi, everyone. I'm Li Dinghao

10
00:00:36,280 --> 00:00:37,230
(Li Dinghao, Season 7 Guest)
from Season 7.

11
00:00:37,240 --> 00:00:38,640
Great to see you all again.

12
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:39,320
Hi, everyone.

13
00:00:39,320 --> 00:00:42,120
I'm Wang Yifan from Season 8.

14
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:43,920
(Wang Yifan, Season 8 Guest)
Great to see you again.

15
00:00:44,360 --> 00:00:44,760
Hi, everyone.

16
00:00:44,760 --> 00:00:47,760
(Sun Jingjun, Season 6 Guest)
I'm Sun Jingjun from Season 6.

17
00:00:48,000 --> 00:00:49,880
Glad to be back
watching Heart Signal with you.

18
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,880
So today, besides the three of us,

19
00:00:51,880 --> 00:00:53,640
we've also got a mystery guest.

20
00:00:54,080 --> 00:00:54,920
Who is it?

21
00:00:55,800 --> 00:00:57,080
Let's give them a big hand.

22
00:00:58,160 --> 00:00:58,720
Hi!

23
00:01:01,660 --> 00:01:03,060
(Welcome)
Duo.

24
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:04,020
(So happy)

25
00:01:09,840 --> 00:01:10,400
Hi!

26
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:12,520
Welcome, our new friend.

27
00:01:12,520 --> 00:01:16,160
Hi, everyone.
I'm Ke Ailin, or Duo, from Season 8.

28
00:01:16,160 --> 00:01:19,280
(Ke Ailin, Season 8 Guest)
I'm back to watch it with you.

29
00:01:19,760 --> 00:01:21,400
I heard four of your flights
got canceled.

30
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:22,640
Yeah.

31
00:01:22,640 --> 00:01:24,640
I tried flying from Shanghai,
Hangzhou, and Ningbo.

32
00:01:24,640 --> 00:01:25,920
Every flight got canceled.

33
00:01:25,920 --> 00:01:27,680
Yeah, there was nothing you could do
about the weather.

34
00:01:27,680 --> 00:01:28,120
Yeah.

35
00:01:28,120 --> 00:01:31,680
So I ended up driving here
from Hangzhou.

36
00:01:33,440 --> 00:01:34,360
That must've been a rough trip.

37
00:01:34,360 --> 00:01:35,160
That sounds rough.

38
00:01:35,160 --> 00:01:35,720
That was brutal.

39
00:01:35,720 --> 00:01:36,640
Thanks, guys.

40
00:01:36,660 --> 00:01:37,840
(Finally made it)

41
00:01:37,840 --> 00:01:39,400
I was really looking forward
to you getting here because...

42
00:01:43,600 --> 00:01:45,160
I've been hosting the first half.

43
00:01:45,440 --> 00:01:46,960
(Worth saying twice)
I've been hosting the first half.

44
00:01:47,320 --> 00:01:48,040
I'm an introvert.

45
00:01:48,040 --> 00:01:49,480
I'm basically out of social battery.

46
00:01:49,480 --> 00:01:50,480
You're taking over now.

47
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:52,940
Don't worry. I got this.

48
00:01:53,260 --> 00:01:54,140
(So grateful)

49
00:01:56,880 --> 00:01:58,360
How long has it been
since we left the house?

50
00:01:58,360 --> 00:01:59,480
Me? About a year.

51
00:01:59,840 --> 00:02:00,720
Two years for me.

52
00:02:01,480 --> 00:02:02,320
Three.

53
00:02:02,320 --> 00:02:03,120
I'm a fossil now.

54
00:02:07,240 --> 00:02:09,720
So what has everyone been up to
since leaving the house?

55
00:02:09,920 --> 00:02:13,080
I've just kept doing my design work.

56
00:02:13,720 --> 00:02:15,720
And lately,
I've been putting together a portfolio.

57
00:02:15,720 --> 00:02:17,880
It should be out
by the end of this year.

58
00:02:17,880 --> 00:02:20,400
Go follow Dinghao's account.

59
00:02:20,400 --> 00:02:22,000
(Can't wait)
We'll be looking forward to it.

60
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:24,120
What about you, Jingjun?

61
00:02:24,360 --> 00:02:26,400
I was still doing my master's
when I was on the show.

62
00:02:26,560 --> 00:02:28,640
Now I'm continuing
with the plan I had back then.

63
00:02:28,640 --> 00:02:29,520
I'm doing a PhD.

64
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:31,080
Nice.

65
00:02:31,640 --> 00:02:33,680
As my friends put it,

66
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:34,800
I've basically become a hermit.

67
00:02:34,800 --> 00:02:36,840
I've kind of lost track of time.

68
00:02:37,320 --> 00:02:37,960
So thanks

69
00:02:37,960 --> 00:02:39,760
for digging this old fossil back up

70
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,000
and bringing me out to see everyone.

71
00:02:41,000 --> 00:02:41,840
It's nice to have some fun.

72
00:02:42,680 --> 00:02:43,840
Three years later,
and you're still a student.

73
00:02:46,960 --> 00:02:47,840
What about Yifan?

74
00:02:48,080 --> 00:02:49,380
I'm still out there every day,

75
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,760
(Hard at work)
on the daily grind.

76
00:02:50,760 --> 00:02:53,040
I've already been working for two years.

77
00:02:53,040 --> 00:02:54,560
But I love watching your vlogs.

78
00:02:54,560 --> 00:02:56,280
Really? You like my daily grind posts?

79
00:02:56,280 --> 00:02:57,320
And here's the thing.

80
00:02:57,320 --> 00:02:58,440
Since we're friends,

81
00:02:58,440 --> 00:03:00,040
I get to see your private posts.

82
00:03:01,360 --> 00:03:02,600
Those are my little secrets.

83
00:03:02,760 --> 00:03:03,080
Right.

84
00:03:03,240 --> 00:03:04,320
What do you post there?

85
00:03:06,120 --> 00:03:07,160
It's way more random.

86
00:03:07,160 --> 00:03:08,280
Just me being unhinged.

87
00:03:08,760 --> 00:03:09,440
Exactly.

88
00:03:09,440 --> 00:03:10,460
Hahaha!
So that's what you're really like.

89
00:03:10,580 --> 00:03:11,100
Hahaha!

90
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:11,700
That's hilarious.

91
00:03:12,040 --> 00:03:12,840
Pretty much.

92
00:03:13,640 --> 00:03:14,960
So what have you been up to, Duo?

93
00:03:15,440 --> 00:03:16,280
I've always been someone

94
00:03:16,280 --> 00:03:17,240
who really enjoys working

95
00:03:17,240 --> 00:03:18,880
and likes staying busy.

96
00:03:19,720 --> 00:03:21,580
I'm also excited to see

97
00:03:21,580 --> 00:03:22,680
(Enjoy today, look ahead)
what changes come next.

98
00:03:25,080 --> 00:03:27,640
Duo, you probably watched

99
00:03:27,640 --> 00:03:28,400
the preview on the way here.

100
00:03:28,400 --> 00:03:29,080
Right?

101
00:03:29,520 --> 00:03:30,450
Yeah.

102
00:03:30,450 --> 00:03:31,680
I thought it was really good.

103
00:03:32,040 --> 00:03:33,240
Like, really, really good.

104
00:03:34,560 --> 00:03:35,280
I'm curious

105
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:36,040
which guest

106
00:03:36,040 --> 00:03:38,320
caught your attention the most?

107
00:03:38,920 --> 00:03:40,440
For me, probably Cui Kaiyi.

108
00:03:40,640 --> 00:03:42,240
She has this bright, sunny energy.

109
00:03:43,200 --> 00:03:45,240
On the guys' side,

110
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:46,520
Cao Yiheng stood out to me.

111
00:03:46,520 --> 00:03:48,280
Because he picked the green card,

112
00:03:48,280 --> 00:03:49,200
just like I did.

113
00:03:49,200 --> 00:03:49,560
Right.

114
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,720
And this season,

115
00:03:51,720 --> 00:03:53,400
he's the only one who picked green.

116
00:03:53,400 --> 00:03:55,120
So, I'm really curious

117
00:03:55,120 --> 00:03:56,920
which girl he'll connect with.

118
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:01,240
I thought Yu Yang and Liang Renfang

119
00:04:01,640 --> 00:04:03,680
had an interesting vibe

120
00:04:03,680 --> 00:04:04,440
when they first met.

121
00:04:04,440 --> 00:04:06,320
So, I'm curious to see

122
00:04:06,320 --> 00:04:07,560
whether sparks start flying.

123
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,240
When I watched it,

124
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:12,840
Yu Yang stood out to me.

125
00:04:13,120 --> 00:04:14,400
I feel like

126
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:15,320
he has this little

127
00:04:15,320 --> 00:04:17,200
unexpectedly goofy side.

128
00:04:17,200 --> 00:04:17,680
Yeah.

129
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:22,200
Oh, right. In the last preview,

130
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,160
we also guessed

131
00:04:23,160 --> 00:04:24,960
who'd get the most attention.

132
00:04:25,120 --> 00:04:26,320
My picks

133
00:04:26,320 --> 00:04:28,160
were Cui Kaiyi and...

134
00:04:28,160 --> 00:04:28,960
Chen Hewen.

135
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,600
(Cui Kaiyi, Chen Hewen)
I thought they'd be the most popular.

136
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:31,520
I picked

137
00:04:31,520 --> 00:04:32,840
Sun Bohan and Cui Kaiyi.

138
00:04:33,160 --> 00:04:34,880
(Sun Bohan, Cui Kaiyi)
They had the biggest smiles.

139
00:04:37,760 --> 00:04:38,800
I picked

140
00:04:39,800 --> 00:04:41,160
Sha Yue'er and...

141
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,320
the guy from the Green Space,

142
00:04:43,320 --> 00:04:44,520
(Sha Yue'er, Cao Yiheng)
Cao Yiheng.

143
00:04:45,080 --> 00:04:46,200
Duo, who did you pick?

144
00:04:46,360 --> 00:04:47,720
For the guys,

145
00:04:47,720 --> 00:04:48,920
I'd guess Sun Bohan.

146
00:04:49,480 --> 00:04:51,120
If I had to pick one girl,

147
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,680
(Sun Bohan, Sha Yue'er)
I'd probably go with Sha Yue'er.

148
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:56,360
She seems really easy to talk to.

149
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:56,640
Yeah.

150
00:04:56,640 --> 00:04:57,920
The way she greets people

151
00:04:57,920 --> 00:04:59,160
is very open and confident.

152
00:04:59,160 --> 00:05:00,640
She doesn't give off

153
00:05:00,640 --> 00:05:02,160
an unapproachable vibe.

154
00:05:02,160 --> 00:05:04,040
You feel comfortable
with her right away.

155
00:05:05,800 --> 00:05:07,440
All right, let's see

156
00:05:07,440 --> 00:05:09,320
who actually got it right.

157
00:05:09,480 --> 00:05:10,440
Here we go.

158
00:05:11,140 --> 00:05:13,420
(Red pocket square)

159
00:05:13,420 --> 00:05:16,060
(Yellow dress)

160
00:05:20,440 --> 00:05:21,120
Here they come.

161
00:05:21,210 --> 00:05:21,930
Here?

162
00:05:22,660 --> 00:05:23,590
Hello.

163
00:05:23,770 --> 00:05:25,650
We didn't meet yesterday, right?

164
00:05:26,810 --> 00:05:27,650
(Double handshake)
Hello. I'm Chen Hewen.

165
00:05:27,650 --> 00:05:28,200
Chen Hewen seems

166
00:05:28,200 --> 00:05:29,640
really proactive.

167
00:05:29,920 --> 00:05:30,280
Yeah.

168
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,180
Go ahead, pick a seat.

169
00:05:31,180 --> 00:05:32,450
Why don't you sit first?

170
00:05:32,450 --> 00:05:32,660
Sure.

171
00:05:32,670 --> 00:05:33,240
Go ahead, pick a seat.

172
00:05:33,240 --> 00:05:34,240
Why don't you sit first?

173
00:05:35,760 --> 00:05:36,340
Hello,

174
00:05:36,340 --> 00:05:36,890
Zhao Xilun.

175
00:05:36,890 --> 00:05:38,130
Hello.

176
00:05:38,130 --> 00:05:38,850
Looking sharp today.

177
00:05:38,860 --> 00:05:40,520
The guys warmed up to each other fast.

178
00:05:40,920 --> 00:05:41,680
Yeah.

179
00:05:42,130 --> 00:05:43,010
Top-tier service.

180
00:05:47,920 --> 00:05:49,440
A woman in red.

181
00:05:51,300 --> 00:05:53,780
Hello.

182
00:05:53,780 --> 00:05:55,020
(First-impression picks)

183
00:05:57,660 --> 00:05:59,660
(Looking closely)

184
00:06:00,760 --> 00:06:01,800
I need a magnifying glass.

185
00:06:02,280 --> 00:06:03,680
This is important.

186
00:06:03,680 --> 00:06:05,400
(Sha Yue'er: Zhao Xilun, Cui Yihang,
Chen Hewen, Yu Yang)

187
00:06:05,400 --> 00:06:06,760
I got it right!

188
00:06:07,120 --> 00:06:07,760
Nice.

189
00:06:08,840 --> 00:06:09,320
That's impressive.

190
00:06:09,320 --> 00:06:09,960
Yeah.

191
00:06:11,690 --> 00:06:12,580
Sorry to keep you waiting.

192
00:06:14,070 --> 00:06:15,660
Hello, Sha Yue'er.

193
00:06:16,660 --> 00:06:18,210
Hello, Sha Yue'er.

194
00:06:18,230 --> 00:06:19,080
They know each other?

195
00:06:19,080 --> 00:06:19,960
Pretty well.

196
00:06:19,960 --> 00:06:20,600
Pretty well, huh?

197
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,800
He's striding right in.

198
00:06:22,840 --> 00:06:23,520
Sun Bohan.

199
00:06:24,040 --> 00:06:25,480
It's his first time meeting Sha Yue'er.

200
00:06:25,480 --> 00:06:26,000
Have a seat.

201
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:26,700
Let's not...

202
00:06:26,700 --> 00:06:27,500
(Hits the planter)

203
00:06:27,500 --> 00:06:28,080
Careful!

204
00:06:30,500 --> 00:06:31,150
Careful!

205
00:06:32,500 --> 00:06:33,070
Sorry.

206
00:06:33,700 --> 00:06:35,080
Let's sit.

207
00:06:35,450 --> 00:06:36,490
I'm Sha Yue'er.

208
00:06:36,490 --> 00:06:38,260
That's a really uncommon last name.

209
00:06:39,200 --> 00:06:40,000
(Sha Yi.)
It is.

210
00:06:41,280 --> 00:06:42,080
Don't you think...

211
00:06:42,080 --> 00:06:43,120
He's dying to talk to Sha Yue'er.

212
00:06:43,120 --> 00:06:43,840
Don't you think Chen Hewen

213
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:44,880
looks a little like Jingjun?

214
00:06:45,320 --> 00:06:46,520
I was just going to say that.

215
00:06:47,320 --> 00:06:49,320
You really do look a bit
like Chen Hewen.

216
00:06:49,320 --> 00:06:50,600
(Extrovert version)
We've got the extrovert there,

217
00:06:50,600 --> 00:06:51,520
(Introvert version)
and the introvert

218
00:06:51,520 --> 00:06:52,280
is right here with us.

219
00:06:52,280 --> 00:06:53,960
It feels so surreal.

220
00:06:56,640 --> 00:06:57,440
Just kidding.

221
00:06:57,800 --> 00:06:59,000
You're all good.

222
00:06:59,810 --> 00:07:01,540
Did any word stand out to you?

223
00:07:01,540 --> 00:07:02,150
Something you liked,

224
00:07:02,150 --> 00:07:03,660
or maybe didn't like as much?

225
00:07:03,840 --> 00:07:04,700
Yeah.

226
00:07:04,700 --> 00:07:05,460
Probably this one.

227
00:07:05,460 --> 00:07:08,370
I think we picked...

228
00:07:08,440 --> 00:07:09,520
The way he said it

229
00:07:09,520 --> 00:07:10,680
does feel kind

230
00:07:10,680 --> 00:07:12,120
of different from...

231
00:07:12,680 --> 00:07:13,840
I think Chen Hewen

232
00:07:13,840 --> 00:07:15,120
and Sun Bohan

233
00:07:15,120 --> 00:07:16,520
are both really

234
00:07:16,520 --> 00:07:17,040
proactive.

235
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:17,400
It's obvious.

236
00:07:17,400 --> 00:07:17,880
Yeah.

237
00:07:17,880 --> 00:07:18,840
Yeah, the signals.

238
00:07:19,000 --> 00:07:19,800
I'm really curious

239
00:07:19,800 --> 00:07:21,320
to see what he does next.

240
00:07:21,560 --> 00:07:22,240
Yeah.

241
00:07:22,840 --> 00:07:24,000
Jingjun, if you were in this situation

242
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:25,360
right now...

243
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,600
What would you do?

244
00:07:29,440 --> 00:07:30,880
When everyone suddenly goes quiet,

245
00:07:30,880 --> 00:07:32,600
that's when you need to step up.

246
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:34,320
At the same time, though,

247
00:07:34,320 --> 00:07:35,520
you also need to listen.

248
00:07:35,520 --> 00:07:37,720
I'd probably try to learn more
about her,

249
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:39,680
then wait for the right moment

250
00:07:39,680 --> 00:07:42,200
to show where we click.

251
00:07:43,480 --> 00:07:46,040
You've definitely thought this through.

252
00:07:46,420 --> 00:07:47,860
(Busted)

253
00:07:49,240 --> 00:07:50,680
Let's hear what everyone else would do.

254
00:07:50,680 --> 00:07:51,000
Sure.

255
00:07:51,000 --> 00:07:52,240
(Strategy time)
Dinghao, you go first.

256
00:07:52,240 --> 00:07:53,280
Why me again?

257
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:57,440
I'm pretty similar to Jingjun.

258
00:07:57,440 --> 00:07:59,480
I wouldn't let the room go dead.

259
00:07:59,480 --> 00:08:00,680
If we ran out of things to talk about,

260
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:02,440
I'd bring up a new topic myself.

261
00:08:02,680 --> 00:08:04,360
But honestly, I doubt that'd happen.

262
00:08:04,800 --> 00:08:07,040
I'm probably one of the quieter ones.

263
00:08:07,040 --> 00:08:08,480
Everyone else talks more than I do.

264
00:08:08,480 --> 00:08:09,560
For me,

265
00:08:09,560 --> 00:08:10,480
unless someone

266
00:08:10,480 --> 00:08:13,520
really catches my eye right away,

267
00:08:13,520 --> 00:08:15,800
I'd probably just quietly observe.

268
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:19,760
I'd probably just start off as friends,

269
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:20,960
get to know everyone a little,

270
00:08:20,960 --> 00:08:22,320
and see what they're like.

271
00:08:22,320 --> 00:08:25,240
If I start getting signals
from someone too,

272
00:08:25,240 --> 00:08:27,200
I'd respond.

273
00:08:27,200 --> 00:08:29,800
I might throw out
a few conversation starters.

274
00:08:29,800 --> 00:08:30,920
Yeah, that's probably me.

275
00:08:40,080 --> 00:08:42,640
So Cao Yiheng has the most votes
among the guys.

276
00:08:42,640 --> 00:08:45,300
(Cao Yiheng: Sun Qimeng, Wu Siying)
Yeah, Cao Yiheng is number one.

277
00:08:45,320 --> 00:08:46,440
I got it right.

278
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,040
You got both right.

279
00:08:48,040 --> 00:08:49,040
That's seriously impressive.

280
00:08:50,620 --> 00:08:51,700
(So happy)

281
00:08:51,920 --> 00:08:53,720
Nice, Yifan!

282
00:08:53,720 --> 00:08:54,520
Seriously impressive.

283
00:08:54,760 --> 00:08:56,040
I'm a psychic.

284
00:08:56,040 --> 00:08:57,160
Congrats, Yifan.

285
00:08:57,160 --> 00:08:59,920
You win our Heart Signal pillow.

286
00:09:00,360 --> 00:09:01,260
Come on, award ceremony.

287
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:02,360
(Visit WeTV Grassland Hub
for merch and collectibles)

288
00:09:02,360 --> 00:09:03,160
Thank you.

289
00:09:03,360 --> 00:09:04,040
Congrats.

290
00:09:04,040 --> 00:09:04,560
Congrats, Yifan.

291
00:09:05,920 --> 00:09:07,200
Am I the first person

292
00:09:07,200 --> 00:09:08,680
to own Season 9 merch?

293
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:09,680
Yes.

294
00:09:09,680 --> 00:09:10,760
I think I need to keep learning.

295
00:09:11,440 --> 00:09:12,280
There he goes studying again.

296
00:09:12,760 --> 00:09:13,920
Research and take notes.

297
00:09:16,990 --> 00:09:18,980
So you two met yesterday?

298
00:09:19,450 --> 00:09:20,020
Yeah.

299
00:09:20,020 --> 00:09:22,000
We talked for about 20 minutes
at the end.

300
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:26,660
I think they were probably
a little surprised

301
00:09:26,660 --> 00:09:27,420
when I showed up.

302
00:09:28,260 --> 00:09:29,470
Not really.

303
00:09:30,020 --> 00:09:31,160
Everyone was waiting for you.

304
00:09:32,360 --> 00:09:34,040
"Everyone was waiting for you".

305
00:09:34,720 --> 00:09:35,860
That's such a sweet thing to say.

306
00:09:35,860 --> 00:09:37,180
(Shy)

307
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:38,660
Were you hoping

308
00:09:38,660 --> 00:09:40,260
to meet a certain type of person
in the house?

309
00:09:40,260 --> 00:09:41,060
(Who are they hoping to meet?)

310
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:43,420
Someone who looks well-groomed.

311
00:09:44,800 --> 00:09:45,680
She sneaks a glance.

312
00:09:45,680 --> 00:09:47,960
She's watching his reaction.

313
00:09:48,690 --> 00:09:50,590
Fresh-faced, kind of artsy?

314
00:09:51,550 --> 00:09:52,540
That kind of vibe?

315
00:09:53,060 --> 00:09:54,420
(Slight smile)

316
00:09:55,800 --> 00:09:57,500
All I can say is,
she asked the right question.

317
00:09:57,500 --> 00:09:58,180
(Holding it in)

318
00:09:59,190 --> 00:10:00,840
That kind of vibe?

319
00:10:00,840 --> 00:10:01,410
Yeah, pretty much.

320
00:10:01,560 --> 00:10:02,760
That's exactly what he wanted to hear.

321
00:10:05,570 --> 00:10:07,790
What about personality?

322
00:10:07,790 --> 00:10:08,640
Anything you look for?

323
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:12,560
Two extroverts

324
00:10:12,560 --> 00:10:13,560
(Stepping in to help)
picking on one introvert.

325
00:10:13,560 --> 00:10:14,360
He bailed her out.

326
00:10:14,760 --> 00:10:16,460
Was it boring waiting here so long?

327
00:10:16,460 --> 00:10:17,780
(Takes the initiative)

328
00:10:18,240 --> 00:10:19,200
And now they're one-on-one.

329
00:10:19,200 --> 00:10:21,480
(Looks over)
Not really. You guys are all here now.

330
00:10:21,480 --> 00:10:22,560
He's used to waiting.

331
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:23,910
Very emotionally steady.

332
00:10:23,910 --> 00:10:25,900
But today's a little different
from yesterday.

333
00:10:25,900 --> 00:10:26,530
Today,

334
00:10:26,530 --> 00:10:27,890
someone finally joined me on my turf.

335
00:10:29,450 --> 00:10:30,640
(Instant response)
The color.

336
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:32,600
She gets what he means.

337
00:10:32,600 --> 00:10:33,920
Yeah, she totally gets it.

338
00:10:34,870 --> 00:10:35,870
(Explaining for him)
Didn't he choose green yesterday?

339
00:10:35,870 --> 00:10:37,520
(Surrounded by green)
All the plants are green.

340
00:10:38,560 --> 00:10:39,280
Good catch.

341
00:10:40,270 --> 00:10:40,910
Here it comes.

342
00:10:42,120 --> 00:10:43,200
Another message.

343
00:10:43,200 --> 00:10:44,080
A text.

344
00:10:44,690 --> 00:10:45,830
Go to the main dinner venue

345
00:10:45,830 --> 00:10:47,140
and meet everyone.

346
00:10:47,200 --> 00:10:48,240
So this isn't even the main venue?

347
00:10:48,400 --> 00:10:49,580
They're all going to meet again.

348
00:10:49,580 --> 00:10:51,020
(Dinner officially begins)

349
00:10:51,040 --> 00:10:51,560
Dinner.

350
00:10:51,560 --> 00:10:52,440
Still at a long table.

351
00:10:52,600 --> 00:10:54,200
But there is one great thing
about a long table.

352
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:56,120
If the person you like
is right next to you,

353
00:10:56,120 --> 00:10:57,160
it's really easy to create...

354
00:10:57,160 --> 00:10:58,640
Your own little conversation bubble.

355
00:10:58,640 --> 00:10:59,240
Exactly.

356
00:11:03,480 --> 00:11:04,760
They've got such a presence.

357
00:11:05,440 --> 00:11:05,940
So many...

358
00:11:05,960 --> 00:11:06,480
People.

359
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:07,040
So many.

360
00:11:07,280 --> 00:11:08,920
So many people.

361
00:11:09,250 --> 00:11:10,510
Can I sit here?

362
00:11:10,970 --> 00:11:11,660
Sure.

363
00:11:11,880 --> 00:11:12,680
Sun Bohan.

364
00:11:12,680 --> 00:11:15,240
Is he going to sit beside her
or across from her?

365
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:17,880
I think he's going across.

366
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:19,080
Then I'll sit here.

367
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,820
(Across from Sha Yue'er)
He's already made it clear.

368
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,960
His actions say it all.

369
00:11:23,340 --> 00:11:24,990
Let's introduce ourselves.

370
00:11:24,990 --> 00:11:25,500
I'll go first.

371
00:11:25,990 --> 00:11:27,670
Sure. Leader, you go first.

372
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:28,800
Leader?

373
00:11:30,550 --> 00:11:31,710
Can anyone here cook?

374
00:11:32,090 --> 00:11:33,410
A little.

375
00:11:33,890 --> 00:11:35,840
(Follows up)
How little are we talking?

376
00:11:36,640 --> 00:11:37,820
Home cooking.

377
00:11:37,820 --> 00:11:38,400
Home cooking?

378
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:38,830
Like,

379
00:11:38,830 --> 00:11:39,690
braised fish

380
00:11:39,690 --> 00:11:40,720
and kung pao chicken.

381
00:11:41,150 --> 00:11:42,500
Braised fish counts as home cooking?

382
00:11:44,880 --> 00:11:46,880
Sun Bohan is really good at keeping
the conversation going.

383
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:47,200
Yeah.

384
00:11:47,200 --> 00:11:48,880
He never lets anything Sha Yue'er says

385
00:11:48,880 --> 00:11:50,080
fall flat.

386
00:11:50,080 --> 00:11:50,630
I can do simple stuff.

387
00:11:50,630 --> 00:11:51,550
If I follow a recipe,

388
00:11:51,550 --> 00:11:52,540
I can make it.

389
00:11:54,530 --> 00:11:55,720
Probably not as well as you.

390
00:11:55,720 --> 00:11:56,820
(Compliment)
You can make braised fish, after all.

391
00:11:56,880 --> 00:11:58,080
See? That's what he does.

392
00:11:58,080 --> 00:11:59,240
The conversation could've ended there,

393
00:11:59,240 --> 00:12:00,760
but he handed it right back to her.

394
00:12:06,570 --> 00:12:08,890
(Rules Message)
Profiles will now be revealed.

395
00:12:08,890 --> 00:12:10,110
Go to one opposite-sex guest's chair.

396
00:12:10,120 --> 00:12:10,880
So basically,

397
00:12:10,880 --> 00:12:12,400
you have to go get their profile card.

398
00:12:12,400 --> 00:12:13,080
That's pretty direct.

399
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,160
So direct.

400
00:12:14,160 --> 00:12:14,960
This is intense.

401
00:12:14,960 --> 00:12:16,600
If someone takes a card...

402
00:12:16,600 --> 00:12:17,360
Then no one else can take it.

403
00:12:17,360 --> 00:12:18,200
Right, it's gone.

404
00:12:18,200 --> 00:12:19,440
So this really matters.

405
00:12:19,670 --> 00:12:20,340
Why isn't anyone moving?

406
00:12:20,880 --> 00:12:22,000
Who's getting up first?

407
00:12:22,000 --> 00:12:23,640
I think it'll be Leader.

408
00:12:24,120 --> 00:12:25,820
He looks ready to make a move.

409
00:12:25,820 --> 00:12:26,480
I'll go first.

410
00:12:26,480 --> 00:12:27,040
See?

411
00:12:27,040 --> 00:12:27,680
I'll go first.

412
00:12:27,680 --> 00:12:28,240
Leader's up.

413
00:12:28,680 --> 00:12:29,280
(I'll go first.)
There he goes.

414
00:12:29,860 --> 00:12:30,580
Nice!

415
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:31,380
Nice!

416
00:12:33,720 --> 00:12:36,040
Jingjun is fully rooting
for his little bro now.

417
00:12:39,660 --> 00:12:40,980
(Heads right)

418
00:12:41,000 --> 00:12:41,800
He's going toward...

419
00:12:51,720 --> 00:12:52,560
Not smiling anymore, huh?

420
00:12:52,560 --> 00:12:53,280
He can't even smile.

421
00:12:53,280 --> 00:12:54,240
Not feeling smiley?

422
00:12:56,280 --> 00:12:58,840
If you were at this dinner,

423
00:12:58,840 --> 00:13:01,960
would you be the first
to grab someone's card?

424
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,000
I probably would.

425
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:06,120
It's been three years
since I left the house,

426
00:13:06,120 --> 00:13:06,840
so I wonder if I've changed.

427
00:13:06,840 --> 00:13:07,400
But...

428
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:08,960
when I picture myself

429
00:13:08,960 --> 00:13:10,160
in that situation,

430
00:13:10,160 --> 00:13:11,360
I'd probably still do the same thing.

431
00:13:12,800 --> 00:13:13,680
Duo?

432
00:13:13,920 --> 00:13:14,880
Do you even have to ask?

433
00:13:15,840 --> 00:13:17,040
Absolutely.

434
00:13:17,040 --> 00:13:17,680
Same.

435
00:13:17,680 --> 00:13:18,680
Absolutely.

436
00:13:18,680 --> 00:13:20,320
Because with this rule,

437
00:13:20,320 --> 00:13:21,720
once you take someone's card,

438
00:13:21,720 --> 00:13:23,040
no one else can get it.

439
00:13:23,040 --> 00:13:23,480
Right.

440
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:25,280
So, it matters a lot.

441
00:13:27,400 --> 00:13:28,610
You're a trader?

442
00:13:28,610 --> 00:13:29,140
Yeah.

443
00:13:29,950 --> 00:13:31,390
So, Sha Yue'er,
what are your work hours?

444
00:13:31,390 --> 00:13:32,090
Is it a nine-to-five?

445
00:13:32,800 --> 00:13:33,860
Yeah, nine to five.

446
00:13:33,860 --> 00:13:34,800
So your work hours

447
00:13:34,800 --> 00:13:35,430
are pretty fixed.

448
00:13:35,430 --> 00:13:36,470
Do you like

449
00:13:36,470 --> 00:13:37,850
the nine-to-five lifestyle?

450
00:13:38,120 --> 00:13:39,120
Her head keeps turning.

451
00:13:39,120 --> 00:13:39,600
Yeah.

452
00:13:39,600 --> 00:13:40,200
Answer yours first,

453
00:13:40,200 --> 00:13:40,600
then his,

454
00:13:40,600 --> 00:13:41,040
then the next one,

455
00:13:41,040 --> 00:13:41,720
and the last one.

456
00:13:43,320 --> 00:13:43,920
So many questions.

457
00:13:48,620 --> 00:13:50,070
(Cui Kaiyi, Sun Bohan)
I'll introduce myself from here.

458
00:13:50,080 --> 00:13:51,160
Cui Kaiyi took Sun Bohan's card.

459
00:13:51,160 --> 00:13:51,950
You took mine,

460
00:13:51,950 --> 00:13:52,780
so I'll take yours.

461
00:13:53,140 --> 00:13:54,860
(Leans back)

462
00:13:55,240 --> 00:13:56,560
Why are we so excited?

463
00:13:58,280 --> 00:13:59,760
We should be.

464
00:14:00,720 --> 00:14:01,880
I really want a pen.

465
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:03,120
You want to take notes, don't you?

466
00:14:03,120 --> 00:14:03,800
I want to map it all out.

467
00:14:07,640 --> 00:14:08,480
There's a card in the room.

468
00:14:09,520 --> 00:14:11,240
All right, time to take notes.

469
00:14:11,440 --> 00:14:13,200
We're taking
this episode very seriously.

470
00:14:13,200 --> 00:14:13,680
We're keeping track

471
00:14:13,680 --> 00:14:15,460
all the way to the finale.

472
00:14:16,320 --> 00:14:18,200
I need to write down
these mutual picks too.

473
00:14:18,200 --> 00:14:18,880
Let's do it.

474
00:14:21,840 --> 00:14:22,600
Wu Siying is up.

475
00:14:23,040 --> 00:14:24,320
(Wu Siying, Zhao Xilun)
Wu Siying is pretty proactive.

476
00:14:24,320 --> 00:14:25,800
Yeah, she's very clear
about who she likes.

477
00:14:25,800 --> 00:14:26,840
She goes right for it.

478
00:14:28,400 --> 00:14:30,640
Zhao Xilun took Wu Siying's card.

479
00:14:34,160 --> 00:14:36,160
Sun Bohan wanted Sha Yue'er's too.

480
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:37,400
Let's map this out together.

481
00:14:37,400 --> 00:14:38,280
I think it's...

482
00:14:38,480 --> 00:14:41,040
First, this one.

483
00:14:41,460 --> 00:14:44,100
This one.

484
00:14:44,120 --> 00:14:45,840
But I think... What's his name?

485
00:14:47,100 --> 00:14:47,860
This one.

486
00:14:47,940 --> 00:14:48,740
- This one.
- This one too.

487
00:14:48,780 --> 00:14:49,500
- This one.
- And then she...

488
00:14:49,540 --> 00:14:50,380
- Same here.
- Probably like this.

489
00:14:50,420 --> 00:14:50,860
- This one.
- Mm-hmm.

490
00:14:50,860 --> 00:14:51,220
- Yeah.
- This one.

491
00:14:51,260 --> 00:14:54,540
- This one.
- This one.

492
00:14:55,160 --> 00:14:55,640
This one.

493
00:14:55,640 --> 00:14:56,440
But I think that one...

494
00:14:56,440 --> 00:14:58,080
Slow down a little.

495
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,480
Wait, I'm getting lost.

496
00:15:01,080 --> 00:15:01,960
I'm lost.

497
00:15:08,370 --> 00:15:10,640
Choose one person of the opposite sex

498
00:15:10,640 --> 00:15:12,380
(Yu Yang's question)
and hold eye contact for ten seconds.

499
00:15:13,700 --> 00:15:14,820
Oh, I like this.

500
00:15:14,820 --> 00:15:15,540
I love this.

501
00:15:16,020 --> 00:15:17,580
(Looking back and forth)

502
00:15:17,600 --> 00:15:18,440
He gets to choose?

503
00:15:18,440 --> 00:15:19,720
Yeah.

504
00:15:20,320 --> 00:15:21,670
(Excited)
Liang Renfang.

505
00:15:21,670 --> 00:15:22,170
Then...

506
00:15:22,170 --> 00:15:23,060
(Staring)

507
00:15:23,060 --> 00:15:24,220
(10-second stare with Liang Renfang)
See!

508
00:15:25,430 --> 00:15:25,810
Me?

509
00:15:25,920 --> 00:15:26,720
(Okay.)
My ship is sailing!

510
00:15:26,840 --> 00:15:27,880
I've shipped them since Episode 1.

511
00:15:28,300 --> 00:15:29,820
(Scoots over)

512
00:15:35,900 --> 00:15:37,440
I feel
like my heart's about to jump out.

513
00:15:37,440 --> 00:15:37,920
I...

514
00:15:41,810 --> 00:15:43,110
Mine is...

515
00:15:43,670 --> 00:15:46,340
Who do you admire most
among the guys here?

516
00:15:46,340 --> 00:15:47,430
(Sun Bohan's question)
Swap seats with them.

517
00:15:52,040 --> 00:15:53,970
He's not going to switch
with Cui Yihang, is he?

518
00:15:53,970 --> 00:15:54,320
Let's switch.

519
00:15:54,340 --> 00:15:55,380
(Chooses Cui Yihang to swap seats)

520
00:15:55,380 --> 00:15:55,940
Let's switch.

521
00:15:55,960 --> 00:15:56,600
Should be.

522
00:15:56,600 --> 00:15:57,400
Yeah.

523
00:15:57,400 --> 00:15:58,280
He picked Cui Yihang.

524
00:16:04,440 --> 00:16:05,360
Interesting.

525
00:16:06,440 --> 00:16:09,000
So in a situation like that,

526
00:16:09,000 --> 00:16:11,360
if the girl you like is sitting
in the middle,

527
00:16:11,360 --> 00:16:13,040
where would you choose to sit?

528
00:16:13,560 --> 00:16:14,280
Let me think.

529
00:16:14,280 --> 00:16:15,320
Let me picture it.

530
00:16:18,920 --> 00:16:20,120
Probably next to her.

531
00:16:20,320 --> 00:16:20,840
Next to her?

532
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:22,560
Easier to look out for her?

533
00:16:23,200 --> 00:16:24,840
It just feels closer.

534
00:16:25,680 --> 00:16:26,920
Yeah. Sitting across from her

535
00:16:26,920 --> 00:16:28,080
might be easier to talk,

536
00:16:28,080 --> 00:16:29,320
but sitting closer

537
00:16:29,320 --> 00:16:32,320
can create a different kind
of chemistry.

538
00:16:34,160 --> 00:16:34,760
Good point.

539
00:16:34,760 --> 00:16:35,240
It makes sense.

540
00:16:35,240 --> 00:16:37,040
I agree.

541
00:16:37,040 --> 00:16:38,480
(Across +1)
I'd probably sit across from him too.

542
00:16:38,480 --> 00:16:41,360
Sitting across from him,
you can look right at him.

543
00:16:41,360 --> 00:16:42,640
But next to him, you'd be...

544
00:16:42,640 --> 00:16:43,640
(Glances)

545
00:16:43,640 --> 00:16:44,160
Just sneaking little looks.

546
00:16:44,160 --> 00:16:46,100
(Glances)

547
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:48,520
That's true.

548
00:16:48,520 --> 00:16:49,840
But don't you think

549
00:16:49,840 --> 00:16:52,040
sitting next to them
feels more intimate?

550
00:16:52,040 --> 00:16:53,120
Yeah, but if we'd just met,

551
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,080
I'd lean toward sitting across.

552
00:16:54,080 --> 00:16:55,480
Once we knew each other better,

553
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,440
then sitting next
to them might be nicer.

554
00:16:58,400 --> 00:16:59,120
What about you, Duo?

555
00:16:59,320 --> 00:17:02,520
If they're really outgoing,

556
00:17:02,520 --> 00:17:07,040
I'd probably sit next to them.

557
00:17:07,640 --> 00:17:09,200
If they're more introverted,

558
00:17:09,200 --> 00:17:10,960
I'd probably sit across from them.

559
00:17:12,360 --> 00:17:13,480
And you, Jingjun?

560
00:17:16,520 --> 00:17:18,040
In a situation like that,

561
00:17:18,040 --> 00:17:19,040
it's not always

562
00:17:19,240 --> 00:17:21,000
about where I want to sit.

563
00:17:21,000 --> 00:17:21,720
I may not get that seat.

564
00:17:24,480 --> 00:17:25,800
But if I had the chance,

565
00:17:25,800 --> 00:17:27,440
I'd probably sit across.

566
00:17:27,440 --> 00:17:29,240
You get more eye contact that way.

567
00:17:31,560 --> 00:17:34,090
Without saying their name,

568
00:17:34,090 --> 00:17:36,410
(Chen Hewen's question)
use three words to describe

569
00:17:36,410 --> 00:17:37,620
the details you've noticed about her.

570
00:17:37,910 --> 00:17:39,620
Poised, and...

571
00:17:39,620 --> 00:17:40,720
(Poised)

572
00:17:40,720 --> 00:17:41,360
she smiles a lot.

573
00:17:41,620 --> 00:17:42,580
(Smiles a lot)

574
00:17:43,210 --> 00:17:44,670
Also, practical.

575
00:17:46,320 --> 00:17:47,080
That obvious?

576
00:17:51,040 --> 00:17:54,360
I think I see what's going on.

577
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:56,760
Chen Hewen already said

578
00:17:56,760 --> 00:17:58,480
he really believes
in love at first sight.

579
00:17:58,720 --> 00:17:59,080
Right.

580
00:17:59,080 --> 00:18:00,120
So if he's this sure,

581
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:01,560
that means somewhere in this room,

582
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:03,040
he's already felt that spark.

583
00:18:03,240 --> 00:18:03,560
Exactly.

584
00:18:03,560 --> 00:18:05,720
So he needs to be completely open

585
00:18:05,720 --> 00:18:07,560
about his interest and make a move.

586
00:18:07,860 --> 00:18:08,340
Right.

587
00:18:10,120 --> 00:18:11,400
If you got

588
00:18:11,400 --> 00:18:13,040
Chen Hewen's question,
would you answer in a way

589
00:18:13,040 --> 00:18:14,200
that's specific enough

590
00:18:14,200 --> 00:18:15,880
to make it obvious whom you mean?

591
00:18:17,480 --> 00:18:19,440
I think

592
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,640
that basically means

593
00:18:20,640 --> 00:18:22,520
he already knows who he's interested in.

594
00:18:23,120 --> 00:18:24,840
If I were as sure as he is,

595
00:18:24,840 --> 00:18:26,320
I probably would say it too.

596
00:18:26,560 --> 00:18:27,760
So funny.

597
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:28,920
It really depends

598
00:18:28,920 --> 00:18:29,640
on the situation.

599
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:30,600
Yeah.

600
00:18:30,800 --> 00:18:32,740
(Really)
Being practical really matters to me.

601
00:18:32,740 --> 00:18:33,860
(Sincere)

602
00:18:35,360 --> 00:18:37,240
If she hadn't said it,
I might've said it anyway.

603
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:39,960
Or, like Dinghao said,

604
00:18:40,280 --> 00:18:41,920
if I were really sure,

605
00:18:41,920 --> 00:18:43,720
I'd probably say it too.

606
00:18:44,040 --> 00:18:46,320
But other than those two situations,

607
00:18:46,320 --> 00:18:49,560
I don't think I'd be that direct first.

608
00:18:51,440 --> 00:18:52,880
If I could tell

609
00:18:52,880 --> 00:18:54,520
they were clearly interested in me,

610
00:18:54,520 --> 00:18:56,800
I'd be open about it
in front of everyone.

611
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:58,120
I'd let them know I'm interested too.

612
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:00,880
I'd want to give them reassurance

613
00:19:00,880 --> 00:19:02,000
and make my intentions clear.

614
00:19:02,000 --> 00:19:02,680
Got it.

615
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:03,400
I see.

616
00:19:03,800 --> 00:19:04,840
I think I'm the same.

617
00:19:04,840 --> 00:19:07,000
If I'm really interested in someone,

618
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:08,760
I'll probably say it first.

619
00:19:08,920 --> 00:19:10,400
But if I put it out there

620
00:19:10,400 --> 00:19:11,680
and don't get anything back,

621
00:19:11,680 --> 00:19:12,520
I'll let it go.

622
00:19:13,400 --> 00:19:14,000
Yeah.

623
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:15,720
I don't like beating around the bush.

624
00:19:15,720 --> 00:19:17,360
I'm a very direct person.

625
00:19:17,360 --> 00:19:17,760
Right.

626
00:19:20,360 --> 00:19:21,880
Actually, every guest just showed

627
00:19:21,880 --> 00:19:23,600
that they have a pretty clear idea

628
00:19:23,600 --> 00:19:25,920
of the kind of relationship they want.

629
00:19:25,920 --> 00:19:28,000
Did any answer really stand out to you?

630
00:19:30,480 --> 00:19:32,240
I'm still pretty sure about mine.

631
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:33,880
I really like Yu Yang

632
00:19:33,880 --> 00:19:35,080
and his view on relationships.

633
00:19:35,080 --> 00:19:36,680
He said he may not do anything grand,

634
00:19:36,680 --> 00:19:38,840
(Yu Yang)
but he'll remember the little things.

635
00:19:39,720 --> 00:19:42,480
If someone remembers something I said,

636
00:19:42,480 --> 00:19:44,160
it feels like such a nice surprise.

637
00:19:44,160 --> 00:19:45,640
I think a lot of girls

638
00:19:45,640 --> 00:19:48,200
really appreciate those little

639
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:49,600
thoughtful details and surprises.

640
00:19:49,800 --> 00:19:50,360
Yeah.

641
00:19:51,400 --> 00:19:53,480
The ones that stood out to me

642
00:19:53,480 --> 00:19:55,760
were Cao Yiheng and Wu Siying.

643
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:58,560
(Cao Yiheng)
Cao Yiheng said love is armor and softness.

644
00:19:58,560 --> 00:20:00,240
It can make you both gentle and strong.

645
00:20:00,240 --> 00:20:01,640
Wu Siying wrote

646
00:20:01,640 --> 00:20:03,520
(Wu Siying)
that love makes us gentler and braver.

647
00:20:03,520 --> 00:20:05,280
Those two qualities

648
00:20:05,280 --> 00:20:07,280
may seem like opposites,

649
00:20:07,280 --> 00:20:08,580
but in a relationship,

650
00:20:08,580 --> 00:20:09,580
(Having both strength and softness)
having both strength

651
00:20:09,580 --> 00:20:10,960
(is what makes a relationship special)
and softness is what makes it special.

652
00:20:11,320 --> 00:20:12,040
Exactly.

653
00:20:12,840 --> 00:20:13,560
Take your time.

654
00:20:13,560 --> 00:20:14,460
Jingjun,

655
00:20:14,500 --> 00:20:16,620
it's about time for you to go.

656
00:20:19,280 --> 00:20:20,920
I really want to finish watching.

657
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:23,440
But I've got some work to get back to,

658
00:20:23,440 --> 00:20:26,920
so I'll see you guys next time.

659
00:20:26,920 --> 00:20:29,200
Can you text me

660
00:20:29,200 --> 00:20:30,400
what happens later?

661
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:31,720
Of course.

662
00:20:31,720 --> 00:20:33,040
We'll take good notes and fill you in.

663
00:20:33,520 --> 00:20:34,640
All right, I'm heading out.

664
00:20:34,640 --> 00:20:35,840
Okay, Jingjun.

665
00:20:35,840 --> 00:20:36,120
Bye!

666
00:20:36,120 --> 00:20:36,680
Jingjun,

667
00:20:36,680 --> 00:20:37,640
have a safe trip.

668
00:20:37,640 --> 00:20:38,400
Safe travels.

669
00:20:38,400 --> 00:20:39,680
Bye!

670
00:20:40,480 --> 00:20:41,560
See you next time.

671
00:20:41,840 --> 00:20:43,000
Let's keep watching.

672
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:43,800
Sure.

673
00:20:46,380 --> 00:20:47,780
(Signal House)

674
00:20:48,080 --> 00:20:48,440
The villa.

675
00:20:48,440 --> 00:20:49,960
Now this feels different.

676
00:20:50,270 --> 00:20:51,020
Hello.

677
00:20:51,800 --> 00:20:53,400
Hello.

678
00:20:53,400 --> 00:20:53,940
Here are your slippers.

679
00:20:54,020 --> 00:20:54,820
(Gets her the slippers)

680
00:20:56,670 --> 00:20:57,250
Where's your suitcase?

681
00:20:57,780 --> 00:20:58,840
Downstairs.

682
00:20:58,840 --> 00:21:00,560
Who's going to help her get it?

683
00:21:00,920 --> 00:21:02,360
Must be Leader.

684
00:21:04,350 --> 00:21:04,980
We'll go get it for you.

685
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:05,800
(In sync)
See?

686
00:21:05,800 --> 00:21:07,180
(Another one)
How many suitcases do you have?

687
00:21:07,180 --> 00:21:08,090
One.

688
00:21:08,240 --> 00:21:09,170
Just one.

689
00:21:09,170 --> 00:21:09,540
Okay.

690
00:21:17,160 --> 00:21:18,600
He's taking Renfang's picture.

691
00:21:18,700 --> 00:21:19,660
Wow!

692
00:21:19,980 --> 00:21:20,740
Wow.

693
00:21:22,280 --> 00:21:22,960
(Checking)
So natural.

694
00:21:22,960 --> 00:21:25,320
They're being pretty... obvious too.

695
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:26,840
(The expert agrees)
Yeah, we agree.

696
00:21:27,040 --> 00:21:28,580
I agree.

697
00:21:28,880 --> 00:21:30,240
What do you usually listen to
when it rains?

698
00:21:30,400 --> 00:21:31,290
When it rains?

699
00:21:31,930 --> 00:21:32,620
Dan...

700
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:33,380
Daniel Caesar.

701
00:21:33,400 --> 00:21:34,120
(Answers instantly)
Impressive.

702
00:21:34,120 --> 00:21:34,920
That's smooth.

703
00:21:36,060 --> 00:21:37,590
(Their first meeting, Day 1)
What kind of music

704
00:21:37,590 --> 00:21:38,570
do you usually listen to?

705
00:21:39,660 --> 00:21:40,580
Daniel Caesar.

706
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:41,900
(Makes a note)

707
00:21:41,920 --> 00:21:43,040
See?

708
00:21:43,040 --> 00:21:44,200
(Yep)
There it is.

709
00:21:44,200 --> 00:21:44,800
I knew it.

710
00:21:44,800 --> 00:21:46,140
(Certified shipper)

711
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:47,600
Back on Day 1,

712
00:21:47,600 --> 00:21:49,400
that was their first time meeting.

713
00:21:49,400 --> 00:21:50,920
And he kept watching her,

714
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:52,240
quietly taking mental notes.

715
00:21:52,240 --> 00:21:55,170
Yeah, I think
they're being pretty obvious too.

716
00:21:56,310 --> 00:21:57,300
Want some water?

717
00:21:58,140 --> 00:21:59,620
(Signals with his eyes)

718
00:22:00,290 --> 00:22:01,240
Yeah.

719
00:22:01,240 --> 00:22:02,800
Why don't we go get some water?

720
00:22:03,260 --> 00:22:04,340
(Pulls her along)

721
00:22:05,360 --> 00:22:06,040
Let's get some water.

722
00:22:06,330 --> 00:22:06,800
Sure.

723
00:22:07,920 --> 00:22:08,800
Me too.

724
00:22:09,040 --> 00:22:09,920
I didn't really get it.

725
00:22:11,360 --> 00:22:11,680
Doesn't matter.

726
00:22:11,680 --> 00:22:13,000
If someone next to you pulls you away,

727
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:14,320
you just go.

728
00:22:14,320 --> 00:22:15,840
You don't even need to understand why.

729
00:22:15,940 --> 00:22:16,700
Oh.

730
00:22:19,240 --> 00:22:20,880
And that leaves just the two of them.

731
00:22:22,080 --> 00:22:23,200
Is it really that obvious?

732
00:22:24,080 --> 00:22:25,080
At that moment,

733
00:22:25,080 --> 00:22:25,910
I think it was.

734
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:26,340
Yeah.

735
00:22:29,280 --> 00:22:31,200
But do you think those two could match?

736
00:22:34,040 --> 00:22:38,000
Right now, I think the guy
is leaning toward her,

737
00:22:38,000 --> 00:22:39,520
but I'm not sure about the girl.

738
00:22:39,720 --> 00:22:41,720
From Cui Kaiyi's reaction,

739
00:22:41,720 --> 00:22:44,120
I don't think she's realized

740
00:22:44,120 --> 00:22:46,280
Cao Yiheng is interested in her.

741
00:22:47,440 --> 00:22:49,880
I think Cui Kaiyi is also

742
00:22:49,880 --> 00:22:50,520
a slow-burn kind of person.

743
00:22:50,520 --> 00:22:51,760
She's a little oblivious.

744
00:22:51,760 --> 00:22:54,080
She may still be treating everyone
as friends.

745
00:22:54,080 --> 00:22:55,720
So Cui Kaiyi may not even realize

746
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:56,480
that someone

747
00:22:56,480 --> 00:22:58,280
is already watching her closely.

748
00:22:59,760 --> 00:23:01,960
But from what I've noticed,

749
00:23:02,240 --> 00:23:03,840
from Day 1 to Day 2,

750
00:23:03,960 --> 00:23:05,480
Cao Yiheng has been

751
00:23:05,480 --> 00:23:08,240
around her a lot.

752
00:23:08,240 --> 00:23:10,320
Maybe you can't tell
if someone actually likes you,

753
00:23:10,320 --> 00:23:11,680
but you can usually feel

754
00:23:11,680 --> 00:23:14,160
that there's at least something there.

755
00:23:14,160 --> 00:23:16,120
Yeah. So from here,

756
00:23:16,120 --> 00:23:19,040
it really depends on how Cao Yiheng acts
and expresses himself.

757
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:20,520
Right. That's important.

758
00:23:20,520 --> 00:23:21,960
Otherwise, she might stay clueless
the whole time.

759
00:23:25,390 --> 00:23:26,180
Step it up,

760
00:23:26,180 --> 00:23:26,790
Meng.

761
00:23:28,210 --> 00:23:29,090
Xilun,

762
00:23:29,090 --> 00:23:30,530
want to go for a walk?

763
00:23:31,040 --> 00:23:32,240
She just said it.

764
00:23:33,040 --> 00:23:34,000
She wants to ask him out.

765
00:23:34,200 --> 00:23:35,000
Yeah.

766
00:23:35,420 --> 00:23:35,950
Hello.

767
00:23:36,560 --> 00:23:37,520
Xilun's right there.

768
00:23:38,320 --> 00:23:39,440
She's seriously brave.

769
00:23:40,160 --> 00:23:40,960
(Turns to look)
Go.

770
00:23:41,480 --> 00:23:42,000
Go for it!

771
00:23:42,000 --> 00:23:43,500
(Go, Meng!)

772
00:23:43,500 --> 00:23:44,730
I need to tell you something.

773
00:23:45,440 --> 00:23:46,000
Uh-oh.

774
00:23:47,520 --> 00:23:48,620
Look.

775
00:23:49,540 --> 00:23:51,220
(He just got water,
and she was called away)

776
00:23:51,240 --> 00:23:52,040
Oh no.

777
00:23:53,840 --> 00:23:55,480
But with a third person standing there,

778
00:23:55,480 --> 00:23:57,240
isn't that kind of hard to say?

779
00:23:57,440 --> 00:23:58,680
I think that was really brave.

780
00:23:59,160 --> 00:23:59,720
Yeah.

781
00:23:59,720 --> 00:24:01,200
That move just now

782
00:24:01,200 --> 00:24:03,240
might be totally outside
her comfort zone.

783
00:24:03,920 --> 00:24:05,200
I think she did great.

784
00:24:05,400 --> 00:24:05,880
Yeah.

785
00:24:07,610 --> 00:24:09,400
Do you prefer Chinese history
or world history?

786
00:24:09,860 --> 00:24:10,640
Both.

787
00:24:10,640 --> 00:24:11,150
Both?

788
00:24:11,380 --> 00:24:13,820
But I mostly know modern world history.

789
00:24:14,020 --> 00:24:15,010
(Looks over)
That's enough.

790
00:24:15,010 --> 00:24:15,740
After World War II...

791
00:24:15,740 --> 00:24:17,950
Because so much of it ties
into economics and politics.

792
00:24:17,950 --> 00:24:19,630
That's pretty close
to your field, isn't it?

793
00:24:19,630 --> 00:24:20,240
(Watching)
Yeah.

794
00:24:20,240 --> 00:24:21,120
I'm dying.

795
00:24:21,120 --> 00:24:22,100
I feel like I'm in class.

796
00:24:22,100 --> 00:24:22,700
(Chen Hewen leaves the study)

797
00:24:22,700 --> 00:24:23,990
They're discussing

798
00:24:23,990 --> 00:24:24,840
modern history.

799
00:24:25,860 --> 00:24:27,920
Modern history?

800
00:24:28,280 --> 00:24:30,200
Kaiyi looks totally lost.

801
00:24:31,500 --> 00:24:32,530
Do you know anyone from our school?

802
00:24:32,530 --> 00:24:33,190
I do.

803
00:24:33,190 --> 00:24:34,240
From your major.

804
00:24:34,240 --> 00:24:36,100
That's why I asked you that day.

805
00:24:36,100 --> 00:24:37,260
(Mr. Spy: The Foolproof Killer)

806
00:24:37,300 --> 00:24:38,500
(Mr. Spy)

807
00:24:39,600 --> 00:24:41,000
The foolproof killer.

808
00:24:41,000 --> 00:24:41,680
I'm dying.

809
00:24:42,240 --> 00:24:43,320
Yue'er is in the study,

810
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:46,480
and then all the guys
slowly start drifting in.

811
00:24:46,760 --> 00:24:48,800
If that were you,

812
00:24:48,800 --> 00:24:49,720
would you go in?

813
00:24:50,520 --> 00:24:52,000
I'd probably pop in

814
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:53,320
to see what's going on,

815
00:24:53,560 --> 00:24:54,680
then leave.

816
00:24:55,400 --> 00:24:57,440
Even if the girl in there
was someone you liked?

817
00:24:57,500 --> 00:24:59,100
(Well...)

818
00:24:59,280 --> 00:25:00,000
That's different.

819
00:25:00,000 --> 00:25:00,960
Dinghao,

820
00:25:01,400 --> 00:25:02,520
you'd go?

821
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:04,120
Then all bets are off.

822
00:25:09,320 --> 00:25:10,880
If you were Yue'er,

823
00:25:10,880 --> 00:25:12,560
with that many people around,

824
00:25:12,560 --> 00:25:15,120
what kind of guy would stand out to you?

825
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:18,160
In that kind of setting,

826
00:25:18,280 --> 00:25:21,120
if someone could keep
the conversation flowing with me,

827
00:25:21,120 --> 00:25:23,840
I'd probably talk to him more.

828
00:25:24,640 --> 00:25:26,880
Yeah. In a big group like that,

829
00:25:26,880 --> 00:25:27,800
I'd probably be the same.

830
00:25:28,160 --> 00:25:30,160
I'd pay attention
to what we're actually talking about.

831
00:25:30,160 --> 00:25:32,360
A guy you have more in common with

832
00:25:32,360 --> 00:25:33,880
would naturally get more
of your attention?

833
00:25:33,880 --> 00:25:34,960
(Right)
Yeah, exactly.

834
00:25:34,960 --> 00:25:36,760
You still need the conversation
to feel good.

835
00:25:36,760 --> 00:25:38,280
Chemistry in person matters a lot.

836
00:25:39,480 --> 00:25:40,000
Okay.

837
00:25:41,640 --> 00:25:42,440
I once came across a quote

838
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,280
that really stuck with me.

839
00:25:43,780 --> 00:25:45,320
People who are extremely arrogant

840
00:25:45,320 --> 00:25:47,090
are often deeply insecure.

841
00:25:48,260 --> 00:25:49,690
Do you think that describes you at all?

842
00:25:49,690 --> 00:25:51,070
Yeah. Deep down, I'm pretty arrogant.

843
00:25:51,070 --> 00:25:52,070
I often feel like

844
00:25:52,070 --> 00:25:53,400
even the people I'm closest to

845
00:25:53,400 --> 00:25:55,450
can be pretty dumb about some things

846
00:25:55,830 --> 00:25:57,280
or just not very good at them.

847
00:25:57,650 --> 00:25:59,000
But I'm also deeply insecure.

848
